## Solution

**Setup: Galois conjugates.** Let $\alpha = 1+\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3}$. The field $\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{2},\sqrt{3})$ has Galois group of order 4, generated by the sign changes of $\sqrt{2}$ and $\sqrt{3}$. Define the four conjugates:

$$\alpha_1 = 1+\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3},\quad \alpha_2 = 1-\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3},\quad \alpha_3 = 1+\sqrt{2}-\sqrt{3},\quad \alpha_4 = 1-\sqrt{2}-\sqrt{3}.$$

**Extracting the coefficients.** Since $x_n = \alpha_1^n = q_n + r_n\sqrt{2}+s_n\sqrt{3}+t_n\sqrt{6}$, applying each automorphism to this identity gives:

$$\begin{aligned}
\alpha_1^n &= q_n + r_n\sqrt{2}+s_n\sqrt{3}+t_n\sqrt{6},\\
\alpha_2^n &= q_n - r_n\sqrt{2}+s_n\sqrt{3}-t_n\sqrt{6},\\
\alpha_3^n &= q_n + r_n\sqrt{2}-s_n\sqrt{3}-t_n\sqrt{6},\\
\alpha_4^n &= q_n - r_n\sqrt{2}-s_n\sqrt{3}+t_n\sqrt{6}.
\end{aligned}$$

Adding/subtracting these four equations (Fourier inversion on the Klein four-group):

$$\begin{aligned}
q_n &= \tfrac{1}{4}\bigl(\alpha_1^n+\alpha_2^n+\alpha_3^n+\alpha_4^n\bigr),\\
r_n &= \tfrac{1}{4\sqrt{2}}\bigl(\alpha_1^n-\alpha_2^n+\alpha_3^n-\alpha_4^n\bigr),\\
s_n &= \tfrac{1}{4\sqrt{3}}\bigl(\alpha_1^n+\alpha_2^n-\alpha_3^n-\alpha_4^n\bigr),\\
t_n &= \tfrac{1}{4\sqrt{6}}\bigl(\alpha_1^n-\alpha_2^n-\alpha_3^n+\alpha_4^n\bigr).
\end{aligned}$$

**Dominant term.** Numerically,
$$|\alpha_1|\approx 4.146,\quad |\alpha_4|=\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3}-1\approx 2.146,\quad |\alpha_2|=\sqrt{3}+1-\sqrt{2}\approx 1.318,\quad |\alpha_3|=\sqrt{3}-1-\sqrt{2}\approx 0.682.$$

(All are positive except $\alpha_4<0$; in any case $|\alpha_1|$ is strictly the largest.) Hence for $i\in\{2,3,4\}$, $\left|\alpha_i/\alpha_1\right|<1$, so $(\alpha_i/\alpha_1)^n\to 0$ as $n\to\infty$.

**Computing the limits.** Form the ratios, factoring out $\alpha_1^n$:

$$\frac{r_n}{q_n}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\cdot\frac{1-(\alpha_2/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_3/\alpha_1)^n-(\alpha_4/\alpha_1)^n}{1+(\alpha_2/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_3/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_4/\alpha_1)^n}\;\longrightarrow\;\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}=\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2},$$

$$\frac{s_n}{q_n}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\cdot\frac{1+(\alpha_2/\alpha_1)^n-(\alpha_3/\alpha_1)^n-(\alpha_4/\alpha_1)^n}{1+(\alpha_2/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_3/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_4/\alpha_1)^n}\;\longrightarrow\;\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3},$$

$$\frac{t_n}{q_n}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{6}}\cdot\frac{1-(\alpha_2/\alpha_1)^n-(\alpha_3/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_4/\alpha_1)^n}{1+(\alpha_2/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_3/\alpha_1)^n+(\alpha_4/\alpha_1)^n}\;\longrightarrow\;\frac{1}{\sqrt{6}}=\frac{\sqrt{6}}{6}.$$

**Answer.**

$$\boxed{\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{r_n}{q_n}=\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2},\qquad \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{s_n}{q_n}=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3},\qquad \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{t_n}{q_n}=\frac{\sqrt{6}}{6}.}$$

